{
  "dom_id": "step-q280531",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "A car accelerates from rest at the origin with an acceleration of $(3i-4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the car to the origin$(|r|)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$",
  "worked_solution": "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i,\\,a=3i-4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the car after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(2i)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(3i-4j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =8i+8(3i-4j) \\\\  & =8i+24i-32j \\\\  & =(32i-32j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the car to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|32i-32j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(32)^{2}+(-32)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1024+1024} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2048} \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
